[00:04.96] Lonesome Suzie never got the breaks
[00:20.86] She's always losing and so she sits and cries and shakes
[00:34.62] It's hard just to watch her and if I touch her
[00:48.68] Oh, poor Suzie, I'm wondering what to do
[01:03.10] She just sits there hoping for a friend
[01:21.22] I don't fit here but I may have a friend to lend
[01:33.22] Maybe I mistook her but I can't overlook her
[01:49.86] Must be someone who can pull her through
[02:04.40] Anyone who's felt that bad could tell me what to say
[02:19.48] Even if she just got mad she might be better off that way
[02:32.08] And where is all the understanding?
[02:39.06] Her problems can't be that demanding
[02:46.36] Why is it she looks my way
[02:53.24] Every time she starts to cry
[03:04.28] Lonesome Suzie, I can't watch you cry no longer
[03:17.18] If you can use me until you feel a little stronger
[03:29.60] I guess just watching you has made me lonesome too
[03:45.18] Why don't we get together, what else can we do
